					 9th Annual Winchendon Fall Festival  
				 
				 Mark your calendars! Fallfest 2025 will be held on October 11, 2025, from 10 am to 5 pm in downtown Winchendon. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Accounting Office 
				 
				 The Town Accountant's Office provides professional staff expertise for financial planning, accounting, and budgeting. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Animal Control 
				 
				 We are pleased to announce that our shelter is now located at 381 Baldwinville Road Templeton, the previous home of Ahimsa Haven. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Assessor's Office 
				 
				 Find information about the Board of Assessors' Office. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Board of Health 
				 
				 Winchendon has a five-member Board of Health whose members work along with a Health Agent and Health Inspector. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Building Department 
				 
				 The Building Department issues permits and schedules inspections for all building, plumbing, gas fitting, and wiring projects in the Town of Winchendon. The Building Department also upholds and enforces the Town’s zoning by-laws. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Collector / Treasurer 
				 
				 The Collector's Office is responsible for the efficient and timely billing and collection of all monies due the Town including real estate tax, excise motor vehicle tax, personal property tax, and water bill payments. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Emergency Management 
				 
				 Find information related to emergency management. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Fire / EMS 
				 
				 Our mission is to protect life and property through emergency response and non-emergency assistance, and to promote public safety through inspection, enforcement, and education. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Beals Memorial Library 
				 
				 The Beals Memorial Library provides a free and open environment where all may gather for education, culture and information. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Parks & Recreation 
				 
				 Our mission is to enhance the quality of life in our community through vibrant parks and engaging recreational programs. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Planning & Development 
				 
				 The Department of Planning and Development serves as the town’s chief planning and development office. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Police Department 
				 
				 The mission of the Town of Winchendon Police Department is to deliver professional, courteous and unbiased police services to all citizens and visitors of the town. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Public Works 
				 
				 The Public Works Department is made up of several divisions including highway, water/sewer, fleet maintenance, cemeteries and parks, solid waste transfer station, and the wastewater treatment plant. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Re-Broadcast of Public Meetings & Events 
				 
				 Tune in to Winchendon Channel 8 to view at listed times. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Registrar of Voters 
				 
				 Find information about the Registrar of Voters. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 School Department 
				 
				 Welcome to Winchendon Public Schools! 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Winchendon Senior Center 
				 
				 The mission of the Winchendon Council on Aging is to provide our seniors with educational programs, recreational activities, and social services assistance, and to advocate for our seniors while educating the community. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Clerk 
				 
				 The Town Clerk is responsible for recording and certifying all official actions of the Town, and oversees all aspects of voting and elections. Additional responsibilities include posting meetings and issuing licenses. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Manager 
				 
				 The Town of Winchendon is pleased to welcome Bill McKinney as the new Town Manager. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Transfer Station 
				 
				 The Town of Winchendon operates a transfer station that is open to all town residents for their disposal of household waste and recyclables. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Transportation 
				 
				 Volunteer at the Winchendon Senior Center
The Winchendon Senior Center relies on volunteers to help support programs, meals, events, and services that enrich the lives of older adults in our community. Whether you have a few hours a month or can volunteer on a regular basis, your time and talents help create a welcoming, connected, and supportive environment for local seniors. Learn more about volunteer opportunities and how to get involved. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Veterans' Services 
				 
				 The mission of Veterans' Services for the Town of Winchendon is to assist each veteran and their dependents through state and federal benefits. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Winchendon Housing Authority  
				 
				 The Housing Authority shall make studies of the housing needs of the community and shall provide programs to make available housing for families of low income and for elderly person of low income. 
				
			 			 
				 
